  "ingredients": [
    "16 ounce macadamia nuts",
    "4 tablespoon coconut oil",
    "2 tablespoon erythritol (optional)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Measure out the macadamia nuts using a kitchen scale.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-macadamia-nut-butter/#wprm-recipe-50705-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/P1052024.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the nuts into a food processor.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-macadamia-nut-butter/#wprm-recipe-50705-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/P1052026.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Process the nuts as finely as possible. The nuts will begin to rise up the sides of the food processor. Use a silicone spatula to scrape down the sides to get a consistent texture.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-macadamia-nut-butter/#wprm-recipe-50705-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/P1052032.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continue processing the nuts. The natural oils will begin to emerge, creating a creamier mixture.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-macadamia-nut-butter/#wprm-recipe-50705-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/P1052035.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continue scraping down the sides as the nut butter rises up.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-macadamia-nut-butter/#wprm-recipe-50705-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/P1052037.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nut butter is finished once it has a very creamy consistency.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-macadamia-nut-butter/#wprm-recipe-50705-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/P1052038.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add in the coconut oil and erythritol. This will help it become a spreadable mixture that will take on a better texture in the fridge.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-macadamia-nut-butter/#wprm-recipe-50705-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/P1052040.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continue processing the mixture until very smooth and creamy. You can taste and add sweetener, if you prefer a sweeter flavor, or would like to add some other addition.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-macadamia-nut-butter/#wprm-recipe-50705-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/P1052042.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour the nut butter into a container for later use.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-macadamia-nut-butter/#wprm-recipe-50705-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/P1052044.jpg"
    }
  ],
